WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.601
Do you need a will,

2
00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.016
a trust, or both?

3
00:00:05.016 --> 00:00:11.100
Four questions can point you in the right direction.

4
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.943
Question one.

5
00:00:12.943 --> 00:00:15.825
Do you have minor children?

6
00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:18.404
If yes, a will matters,

7
00:00:18.404 --> 00:00:23.100
because it is where you name a guardian.

8
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.839
Question two.

9
00:00:24.839 --> 00:00:27.074
Do you own real estate,

10
00:00:27.074 --> 00:00:29.627
or want to avoid probate?

11
00:00:29.627 --> 00:00:32.677
A funded living trust may help.

12
00:00:32.677 --> 00:00:34.202
In some states,

13
00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:35.869
probate is light,

14
00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.100
so it depends.

15
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.985
Question three.

16
00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:42.936
Do you want control over timing,

17
00:00:42.936 --> 00:00:45.461
like money at certain ages,

18
00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:49.798
or care for a family member with a disability?

19
00:00:49.798 --> 00:00:53.100
A trust gives more control.

20
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.849
Question four.

21
00:00:54.849 --> 00:00:56.892
Is privacy important?

22
00:00:56.892 --> 00:01:00.707
A will becomes a public record in probate.

23
00:01:00.707 --> 00:01:04.100
A trust usually stays private.

24
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.403
Even with a trust,

25
00:01:06.403 --> 00:01:10.227
most people still sign a simple will,

26
00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:12.763
called a pour-over will,

27
00:01:12.763 --> 00:01:16.100
plus powers of attorney.

28
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.059
This is a starting point,

29
00:01:19.059 --> 00:01:20.596
not advice.

30
00:01:20.596 --> 00:01:27.100
Take the plan finder and bring the results to a meeting.
